    "media:imagetext": "LAX 747 TEMPORARY FÉFM NOTES\nFLIGHT CONTROLS .090\nNote #30\nTE FLAP MALFUNCTIONS\nThe trailing edge flaps have dual protective systems, both of which open the\naffected by-pass valves. This is the same valve activated by the alternate\narming switch which deactivates the normal flap operation.\nThe two systems\nare:\na. Asymmetry\nb. Flap Failure\nThe asymmetry shut-off signal is produced by a comparator in the individual\nflap indicator. This compares the signals from the two flap transmitters in\neach flap system. Normal threshhold is approximately at 15°\nof transmitter\nmisalignment.\nNormally, there should be an indicator discrepancy if an\nasymmetric failure has taken place.\nThe comparator is not an inherent part of\nthe indicator synchro system but uses the same input signals. It is mounted in\nthe back end of the instrument case.\nThe flap failure system is a series of three switches on the flap control in\nsynchronization with the flap limit switches in the wheel wells.\ncan actuate by rapid changes in movement of the flap position selector without\nallowing the flaps to follow the selection. To correct this condition, move the\nlever to present flap position and reselect the new position.\nBoth systems receive power from #1 DC\nBus P-12, top row under Flight Control\nSystem labeled \"TE Flap Assym \u0026 Fail.\"\nThis breaker also supplies power to the\nbypass valve if either protective system actuates.\nLoss of power from this\nbreaker does not affect operation of the alternate flap system. Loss of power\ndoes deactivate both protective systems.\n3-19-71\nLAX FLIGHT ENGINEERING\nCRUISING\nGONTRO\n82\nEMERGENCY\nLOADING\nOPERATING\nADMATIONI\nPERFORMANCE\n86 RADIO\n87 SYSTEMS AND DESIG",
